# Bounded card composition fit

The shared scaffold reference-cards overlay supplies one canonical engine, store, simulator and UI composition, also exercised by reference-game. The game supplies supported card records, independently authored printed expectations and setup. It implements the existing original synthetic rules only. It does not define a general LCG, response-window collector or campaign generator.

The adapter uses engine-core, card-language, card-zones, turn-flow, automa, game-store, screens and saves. The executable evidence uses card-harness, traceability and sim-pool. Plan, rendered-text and theme checks retain their normal meaning. A generated folder, a passing bootstrap or a matching receipt without browser execution cannot certify a playable slice.

This fit record describes the assembly contract. It is not an external steward response, an execution result or a production-adoption observation.

- Card configuration and synthetic rules: supported records, independent printed expectations and setup configure the canonical original rule adapter.
- Game verbs: the shared adapter defines hit, heal and owned boost through card-language and existing timing APIs; no separate effect interpreter is introduced.
- Screen: card table: game-specific status, hand text, prompts and log use the existing screens and prompt host.
